[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114365","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114365","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114365.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114365.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Fixes #114339\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Cause\r\n\r\nThe `_range_click_timeout()` callback was calling `get_local_mouse_position()` to determine which item to process. If the mouse moved to a different item between the initial click and the timer callback, the wrong item would be activated.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\nStore the original click position (`range_click_start_pos`) when the range click starts, and use that stored position in `_range_click_timeout()` instead of querying the current mouse position. Also properly `reset range_item_last` and `range_click_start_pos` when the timer stops to prevent stale state.\r\n\r\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114365/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114365/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}